.TH SYSTEM-KEYBOARD-QT 1 "2026-07-20" "MX Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
system-keyboard-qt \- configure X11 keyboard layouts and options
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B system-keyboard-qt
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B system-keyboard-qt
provides a graphical interface for configuring the system keyboard. The main page selects the hardware keyboard, reorders layouts and variants, and adds layouts or variants. The Hotkeys page configures the layout-switch key combination, third-level key, and Compose key.
.PP
The Advanced page configures X keyboard options including LED behavior, Caps Lock behavior, and the Kill X key combination. The selected system keyboard is stored in
.I /etc/default/keyboard
for use on future boots.
.SH OPTIONS
This application has no documented command-line options. The graphical interface provides all operations.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/default/keyboard
System keyboard configuration.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/system-keyboard-qt
Installed HTML help, images, license, and changelog documentation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR setxkbmap (1),
.BR keyboard (5)
.SH AUTHOR
MX Linux contributors.
